WHY
Grouping is derived with useMemo from state, not from the server payload, so add,
edit and delete re-group immediately — including when a change moves a payment
into a different financial year. The component already re-sorts date-descending
on both add and edit, and groupByFinancialYear preserves caller order, so the
within-year order stays correct without a second sort.

The subtotal is gross rent (sum of amount). Fees are shown BESIDE it, never
subtracted: rental_payments.amount is the assessable figure and agent fees are a
deduction in their own right. other_outgoings is deliberately absent from the
divider — it exists for bank reconciliation and is never a deduction, so showing
it here would invite double-counting.

Fees are shown only when above zero, so a property whose agent fees were never
itemised gets a clean divider rather than a misleading '$0 fees'.

The lifetime header figures and the table's own Total row are untouched.

